1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,560
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:21,640
Hey, Sid. Are you going to be all right?

3
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:23,680
Yes, I'm sorry.

4
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:29,560
I should have tried to help you escape too, Lord Death, but the distance was too great.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,680
No, no excuses. I have failed you.

6
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:36,560
No, no. You made the best decision given the circumstances.

7
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:42,920
Still, I can't believe it. Our own Dr. Medusa was a witch this whole time.

8
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:47,740
She was using soul protect. It's the only way she could have hidden from us.

9
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,780
Lord Death, aren't there any techniques we can use to combat the soul protect move?

10
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:54,620
Kill it.

11
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:59,440
If not, then we're basically helpless. How can you fight what you can't see?

12
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:03,060
Our struggle against witches has been going on for centuries.

13
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,720
Over the years, witches have come up with any number of new spells.

14
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:12,780
But for every new spell, maesters and weapons have developed new ways of countering them.

15
00:01:13,460 --> 00:01:16,380
For instance, in order to detect and hunt down witches,

16
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:19,460
maesters were born who had the ability to send souls.

17
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:24,400
But now the witches can counter them by using soul protect.

18
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:27,960
So what we have to do now is develop a new technique.

19
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:31,200
The only way to do that now is to quiche your eyes.

20
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:32,040
What?

21
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:36,820
I suppose there's no point in hiding it anymore.

22
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:40,360
If you shut the lid on something that stinks,

23
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:43,060
all you're really doing is hiding the bad smell.

24
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:49,340
To get rid of it, you have to open the lid back up and dive in.

25
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:52,180
Okay, everyone.

26
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:55,280
Could I have your attention for a moment?

27
00:01:55,280 --> 00:02:01,400
There's a kishin sleeping underneath the DWMA.

28
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:06,680
Uh, I think they may need more than that.

29
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:36,660
I think they may need more than that.

30
00:02:36,680 --> 00:03:06,660
I think they may need more than that.

31
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:36,660
To get rid of it, I think they may need more than that.

32
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:40,600
It all happened before this academy was created.

33
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,060
I'll begin at the beginning.

34
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,080
This is the story of a man.

35
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:47,000
His name was Asherah.

36
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,820
Asherah kept himself covered,

37
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:52,660
wrapping his face in long scarves

38
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:54,760
and layering five shirts on top of each other.

39
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:57,280
He wasn't very good at trusting other people.

40
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:59,020
He didn't confide in anybody.

41
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:04,300
He was basically a big ball of paranoia wrapped up in a dozen scarves.

42
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:11,260
Tell me what happened with the Eastern Witches.

43
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:13,520
Sir, by the time we arrived,

44
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,980
Asherah had slaughtered them all.

45
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:20,060
Asherah was a member of my personal squad.

46
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:23,780
He was by far the best and strongest of all the eight guardians.

47
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:27,580
However, he was also the most frightening one of them all.

48
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,980
Always terrified of something.

49
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,640
Asherah became obsessed with power.

50
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:35,120
Eventually, he broke our most sacred rule

51
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:37,740
and began collecting the souls of humans.

52
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:47,560
And thus, because of him,

53
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:48,680
it was born.

54
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:51,300
The Kishan.

55
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,060
The source of all madness.

56
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:57,120
Hold on.

57
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,980
I thought only weapons could consume souls.

58
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,820
How was Asherah able to eat them?

59
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:04,580
I told you, he was a frightened man.

60
00:05:04,820 --> 00:05:07,060
He was terrified of his partner as well.

61
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:11,020
So, he ate his own weapon.

62
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:12,700
What?

63
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:14,780
How is something like that even possible?

64
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:15,800
You know,

65
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,220
now that I think about it,

66
00:05:18,260 --> 00:05:20,580
I'm not sure he was ever human to begin with.

67
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:23,900
It's possible he's nothing more than the embodiment

68
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:26,180
of something that lies deep within his heart.

69
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,920
Fear, for example.

70
00:05:32,740 --> 00:05:34,720
The underground battle commences.

71
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:37,280
Break through Medusa's vector arrow?

72
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,280
Hey, kid.

73
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:44,240
How did Lord Death seal away this Asherah guy in the first place?

74
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:46,600
My father tore off Asherah's skin,

75
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:48,420
made a tightly sealed bag out of it,

76
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:49,940
and stuffed Asherah inside.

77
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:52,240
Then he rooted his own soul and body

78
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,580
here inside Death City

79
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:55,800
to keep the Kishan from ever breaking free.

80
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,460
And because of that,

81
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,120
Lord Death can never leave the city?

82
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:01,340
What if the seal was broken

83
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:03,100
and the Kishan managed to get free?

84
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:06,240
Would Lord Death be able to go wherever he wanted?

85
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,100
That wouldn't work.

86
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:10,680
Lord Death has attached his soul to this town.

87
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:12,260
I suppose you could even say

88
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:14,060
he's become one with Death City.

89
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:16,360
So it's like he's trapped inside himself.

90
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,520
If he wanted to go somewhere,

91
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:20,900
he'd have to find a way of giving the city legs.

92
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,420
And I don't really see that happening anytime soon,

93
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:23,800
do you?

94
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:25,180
Uh-uh.

95
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:28,460
You can't even imagine how disastrous things will be

96
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:29,800
if the Kishan is revived.

97
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:33,700
It's madness is like a plague.

98
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:48,380
Also, you should know you can't control it.

99
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:51,140
Hell is something you carry around with you.

100
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:54,140
Right inside your weak, flimsy little head.

101
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:55,860
Now come along.

102
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,140
Magnus is waiting for you.

103
00:06:58,720 --> 00:06:59,740
There's no escape.

104
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:02,060
You're like a needle stuck in the grooves of the record

105
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,560
spinning around and around.

106
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:05,300
Yeah, right.

107
00:07:05,440 --> 00:07:06,040
Screw that.

108
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:08,200
Your analogy isn't persuasive.

109
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,600
I mean, look at that needle.

110
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,460
It's jumping around all over the place.

111
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:14,200
I'm waiting for your decision.

112
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:15,600
What's it gonna be, soul?

113
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:18,660
Ah!

114
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:30,460
The city sure is lively.

115
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,840
They really know how to throw a party.

116
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,400
I wanted to go too,

117
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,520
but they said only Academy students were allowed

118
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,660
with their fancy gala.

119
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:39,260
No fair.

120
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,880
Oh, I don't have a job,

121
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:43,640
so I don't have any money to go shopping.

122
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:45,860
There's no choice.

123
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:48,020
I'll just have to go visit this shop guy.

124
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:48,740
He knows me,

125
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,180
so he'll give me something at least.

126
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:58,240
Blair, is that you?

127
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,100
Hi, fish shop guy.

128
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:03,480
Blair, here you go.

129
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:06,120
I saved this fish just for you.

130
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:09,360
Oh, no, fish shop guy!

131
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,940
I would do something like this.

132
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:14,480
What's that?

133
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:28,200
I'll have to take care of those cheeky rats.

134
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,260
It took me forever

135
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:30,960
to find that free source of food.

136
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:40,200
I'll have to take care of those cheeky rats.

137
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,660
We've gone a pretty long way now.

138
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:44,680
Hey, Maka,

139
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:46,120
can you sense any witches up ahead

140
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,220
with that little gift of yours?

141
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:50,220
Their soul protects are probably on right now.

142
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:51,680
Oh, all right.

143
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:52,800
That's lame.

144
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,560
Sensing stuff's the only thing you're half decent at.

145
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,000
You don't even know how to piss me off.

146
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:02,440
What? What?

147
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:03,700
Professor Stein!

148
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:04,060
Yeah?

149
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:06,180
I've got something.

150
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:09,180
It's a soul just beyond those shadows.

151
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:11,480
There's someone there.

152
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,320
I know that soul.

153
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:16,280
I'm sure of it.

154
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:19,480
That nasty, despicable feeling.

155
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:22,720
Papa.

156
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:24,960
I'm not nasty.

157
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:26,240
You're despicable.

158
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:27,760
How did you manage to escape

159
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,160
from the trap they set up there?

160
00:09:29,460 --> 00:09:30,620
When it comes to chasing a woman,

161
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:32,120
no one's faster than I am.

162
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,440
I should have guessed.

163
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:35,420
It is a relief to see you, though.

164
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:37,420
I wasn't sure how much I'd be able to do

165
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,640
without my weapon around.

166
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,640
What do we got?

167
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:42,640
Are they up ahead?

168
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:44,340
Uh-huh.

169
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:46,040
Lying in wait for us.

170
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:48,920
Listen up.

171
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,100
From this point forward,

172
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,560
there's no telling what could happen.

173
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,120
It'd be best for you weapons

174
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,580
not to return to human form

175
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:56,340
during the battle.

176
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:57,700
When you're vulnerable,

177
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:59,460
a single blow could be the end of you.

178
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,160
Right.

179
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:01,880
Okay.

180
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,900
Why are they sitting up there

181
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:05,840
waiting for us?

182
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:07,120
I thought they were on their way

183
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:07,820
to the Kishin.

184
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:09,100
No.

185
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:10,940
They would have left some behind

186
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:11,640
for protection.

187
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,880
Hey, did you hear something?

188
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:17,880
Hear what?

189
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:26,280
Yeah, I heard that.

190
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:28,540
It sounds like footsteps to me.

191
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:30,220
So they're finally showing themselves.

192
00:10:31,100 --> 00:10:32,180
Who's it gonna be?

193
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:34,400
Someone able to defend against

194
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,980
and defeat multiple opponents.

195
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,420
Someone who can attack

196
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:38,960
several people simultaneously.

197
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,340
Someone who will make absolutely sure

198
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:42,620
not to let us through

199
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:43,660
no matter what.

200
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:56,180
How lovely to see you all again.

201
00:10:56,180 --> 00:11:04,940
All right.

202
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:05,860
Here's how I think

203
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:06,800
it's going to break down.

204
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:09,960
For the most part,

205
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:10,740
we can anticipate

206
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:11,840
our enemy's moves.

207
00:11:12,220 --> 00:11:13,140
The first roadblock

208
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:14,280
is going to be Medusa.

209
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,360
The demon sword

210
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,620
will be the second barrier.

211
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:21,060
After that,

212
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:21,840
the remaining two

213
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:22,800
will be making their way

214
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:23,520
to the Kishin.

215
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:26,420
The werewolf Maka

216
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:27,620
and the others fought before

217
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:28,180
is immortal,

218
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:29,400
so he'll be in charge

219
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:30,740
of protecting the black blood

220
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:31,680
at all costs.

221
00:11:32,420 --> 00:11:33,120
Now then,

222
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:34,520
this is what we will do.

223
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:36,260
I'll stay here

224
00:11:36,260 --> 00:11:37,420
and keep Medusa busy.

225
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:39,520
While I'm distracting her,

226
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:40,560
I want the three of you

227
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:41,420
to run past her

228
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:42,520
as quickly as possible.

229
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:43,600
Kid,

230
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:44,760
you're the most mobile

231
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:45,580
of our little army,

232
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:47,200
so you continue on ahead of us

233
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:47,880
after the two

234
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:48,440
who are heading

235
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,260
for the Kishin.

236
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:49,900
Understood.

237
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:51,420
Blackstar,

238
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:52,420
you'll be keeping

239
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,540
the demon sword busy

240
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:54,520
so Kid and Maka

241
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:55,300
can get through.

242
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:56,720
Since you can attack

243
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:57,640
directly with your

244
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:58,320
soul wavelength,

245
00:11:58,560 --> 00:11:59,720
you can do the most damage

246
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,660
to the demon sword.

247
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:01,140
Yeah.

248
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:02,700
Finally, Maka,

249
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:04,440
you run on past Medusa

250
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:05,280
and the demon sword

251
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:06,300
to catch up with Kid.

252
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:07,400
Then you destroy

253
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:08,240
the black blood.

254
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:08,800
Right.

255
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:11,500
There's just one last thing.

256
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:12,340
I want you all

257
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:13,320
to make me a promise.

258
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,440
I want you to promise

259
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,280
not to die.

260
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,980
Can you do that?

261
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,260
Yes, sir.

262
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:22,400
Holding a strategy meeting

263
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,520
right in front of your enemy?

264
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:24,720
Is that really

265
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,680
the best idea?

266
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:26,780
Ah, well,

267
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,060
I guess we'll just have

268
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:28,880
to take our chances,

269
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:29,400
won't we?

270
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,960
Always so stupidly confident,

271
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:32,620
aren't you?

272
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,100
Shall we start

273
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:34,920
the party then?

274
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:36,960
Nick, snake,

275
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,240
Cobra, Cobra.

276
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:39,900
Nick, snake,

277
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,140
Cobra, Cobra.

278
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:41,720
Here we go.

279
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:42,540
Don't worry about

280
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:43,360
getting past her

281
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:43,940
right away.

282
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:45,040
